---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site, catalogueProducts } from "../../data.mjs";
const path = "/guides/choose-a-mailer/";
const title = "Poly Mailers vs Bubble Mailers: Which Fits Your Products?";
const formats = [
  { slug: "poly-mailers", name: "Poly Mailers", construction: "Flexible film without a built-in bubble layer", check: "Soft, non-fragile contents; check usable space, seams and closure" },
  { slug: "poly-bubble-mailers", name: "Poly Bubble Mailers", construction: "Film exterior with an inner bubble layer", check: "Compact packs needing cushioning; test the actual contents and lining" },
  { slug: "metallic-bubble-mailers", name: "Metallic & Holographic Bubble Mailers", construction: "Metallic reflective or holographic exterior with bubble cushioning", check: "A specific surface effect plus cushioning; confirm the finish and packed sample" }
].map(format => ({ ...format, sizeCount: catalogueProducts.find(product => product.slug === format.slug).sizes.length }));
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-10-29", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides & FAQs", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Choose a mailer", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Choose poly, poly bubble or metallic and holographic bubble mailers. Compare 13, 15 and 9 catalogue sizes, fit checks, sample needs and custom quote details." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides &amp; FAQs</a> / Choose a mailer</div><p class="eyebrow">Mailer selection guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Choose a poly mailer for soft, non-fragile goods when a flexible shipping layer is enough. Consider a bubble mailer when a compact item needs cushioning. For fragile, heavy or sharp contents, test the complete pack; a mailer alone may not be enough.</p><p class="muted">By <a href="/about/">Welltroy</a> · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-29">29 October 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#compare">Compare formats</a><a href="#finish">Metallic &amp; holographic</a><a href="#protection">Protection</a><a href="#size">Check the fit</a><a href="#example">See an example</a><a href="#quote">Prepare a quote</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <h2 id="compare">Which Mailer Should I Shortlist?</h2>
    <p><strong>Start with the complete packed item, then choose the construction and exterior.</strong> A plain poly mailer suits many soft, non-fragile orders. A poly bubble mailer adds a cushioning layer. Metallic and holographic bubble mailers add a different exterior appearance; that finish does not establish a higher protection rating.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">Swipe or scroll the table to compare formats and catalogue size counts.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Compare three Welltroy mailer formats"><table><caption class="sr-only">Welltroy mailer constructions, catalogue outer-size counts and sample checks</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Format / product details</th><th scope="col">Construction</th><th scope="col">Catalogue outer sizes</th><th scope="col">Check with your sample</th></tr></thead><tbody>{formats.map(format => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={'/products/'+format.slug+'/'}>{format.name}</a></th><td>{format.construction}</td><td>{format.sizeCount}</td><td>{format.check}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="muted">Counts come from the 2025 Welltroy catalogue. They count listed outer-size references, not usable inner sizes, stock availability or every possible custom configuration. Confirm the selected size, material and minimum quantity in the quotation.</p>
    <h2 id="finish">When Should I Choose a Metallic or Holographic Bubble Mailer?</h2>
    <p><strong>Choose this range when the exterior effect is part of your brand brief and a bubble-lined format suits the complete pack.</strong> Welltroy supplies both metallic reflective and holographic surfaces, with samples available for both. Send a reference for the exact effect, then confirm usable space, film structure, print appearance, liner and closure.</p>
    <p>A reflective metallic surface does not by itself establish a holographic effect. Compare the <a href="/guides/metallic-vs-holographic-bubble-mailers/">metallic and holographic finish guide</a> and request the <a href="/products/metallic-bubble-mailers/">offered product and sample details</a>. For a paper exterior, compare <a href="/guides/kraft-vs-poly-bubble-mailers/">kraft and poly bubble mailers</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="protection">Does a Bubble Mailer Replace a Shipping Box?</h2>
    <p><strong>It depends on the product and complete packing method.</strong> A bubble layer adds cushioning but does not establish crush, puncture or transit performance for every item. Share the actual contents, retail box, weight, edges and delivery route. For fragile, heavy, sharp or crushable items, ask whether additional protection or a rigid box is needed and test the proposed complete pack.</p>
    <p>Review the <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#bubble-mailer-cases">two Welltroy bubble mailer customer cases</a> for different material and artwork briefs. Each is a separate configuration, not a protection rating for a new order.</p>
    <h2 id="size">Measure the Packed Item, Then Check Usable Space</h2>
    <ol><li>Pack the item as you will ship it, including any inner bag, box or wrap. Measure its widest width, longest length and greatest thickness.</li><li>Allow room to insert it and close the flap without squeezing the contents or stressing the seal.</li><li>Use catalogue sizes to shortlist models, then ask us to confirm usable inner dimensions, flap allowance, tolerance and current availability. Catalogue dimensions are outer dimensions.</li><li>Test a physical sample with the actual contents and your normal packing process before placing a bulk order.</li></ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Shipping clothing?</strong> Use our <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/">clothing mailer size guide</a> for a measurement checklist and a P03/P04/P05 catalogue example.</div>
    <h2 id="example">Worked Example: A Folded Garment</h2>
    <p>Suppose a garment in its inner bag measures 24 × 30 × 4 cm when packed. Catalogue model P03 is listed as 25 × 30 + 5 cm outside (width × length + flap). Its nominal width and length leave almost no allowance even before accounting for seams and thickness, so it is a poor starting candidate. P04 is listed as 28 × 37 + 5 cm outside and may be worth checking, but those figures do not prove the garment fits. Request usable inner size and test the sealed sample. See the <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/">full size walkthrough</a>.</p>
    <p>For a boxed or rigid item, ask whether a bubble mailer provides enough protection in a complete transit test. A fragile, heavy, sharp or crushable item may need a box or additional packaging.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">What to Send for a Useful Recommendation</h2>
    <ul><li>Contents, existing packaging, and dimensions and weight after packing.</li><li>Breakage, scratch, puncture or moisture concerns and the intended shipping route.</li><li>Quantity for each size and design, material or film preferences, closure and print artwork.</li><li>Destination and required timing; request a sample to check fit and handling.</li></ul>
    <p>If you want to compare two formats, ask for both against the same packed item and quantity. Use the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">quote comparison worksheet</a> to compare material, usable dimensions, print setup, sample route and delivery scope. Keep the <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/">approved sample record</a> with the final quotation.</p>
    <p><strong>Can I start with 500 pieces?</strong> Eligible specifications in the three main mailer ranges start from 500 pieces per confirmed size, color and design. Ask us to confirm your exact configuration; splitting 500 pieces across versions does not automatically meet each minimum. See the <a href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">500-piece enquiry checklist</a> and <a href="/ordering/">design, sample and delivery terms</a>.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Ask us to compare mailers</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Explore products</p><h2>Related Mailers</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Flexible outer shipping for soft goods</span></a><a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Compare cushioning and usable inner space</span></a><a href="/products/metallic-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Metallic &amp; Holographic Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Compare both finishes and request samples</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">Prepare a custom quote brief →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:110px;vertical-align:top}.article-main th[scope="row"]{min-width:125px;vertical-align:top}.article-main table{min-width:650px}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
